            <div xml:id="d832">

                <pb facs="0684" n="568" sameAs="frus:frus1914/pg568"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 812.00/12586.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the
                            Brazilian Minister to Mexico.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1914-07-23">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">July 23, 1914</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>170. Answering your No. 94, July 22, please say to Carbajal we think it would be
                    unwise for him to suggest that negotiations take place in New York. It is
                    important that an agreement should be reached as early as possible and in order
                    to save time we advise him to comply with suggestion made by Carranza and send
                    his delegates directly to Saltillo as soon as possible.</p>
                <p>We are urging upon Carranza and Villa the importance of amnesty and shall
                    continue to use our good offices to this end. Amnesty is a matter that can be
                    arranged between the delegates of Carbajal and Carranza. It would not be wise to
                    insist upon a promise of amnesty before the delegates are sent. It would hardly
                    be fair to insist upon Carranza denying the statements which are attributed to
                    him. It is safe to assume that he made no such statements. If credence were
                    given to newspaper reports, an agreement would be postponed indefinitely. Please
                    urge the importance of immediate action to the end that a peaceful transfer of
                    authority may be made.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Bryan</hi></signed>.</closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
